{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25598466",
      "title": "Managing a List Of Users via State",
      "sourceHash": "04985099624bfa556d751d50d80b74ecdd62eba733072a91a9432d3379b40756",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.5,
          "end": 3.75,
          "en": "We got a list of users,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.75,
          "end": 5.52,
          "en": "which we feed to users list",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.52,
          "end": 7.23,
          "en": "but it's always an empty array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 7.23,
          "end": 9.24,
          "en": "And that of course is pretty static",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 9.24,
          "end": 11.723,
          "en": "and doesn't lead to any users being output.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 12.67,
          "end": 15.22,
          "en": "Now I wanna make sure that when we click that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 15.22,
          "end": 18.27,
          "en": "add user button and the add user component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 18.27,
          "end": 21.01,
          "en": "we don't just log to the user data here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 21.01,
          "end": 22.53,
          "en": "But instead we really create",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 22.53,
          "end": 25.17,
          "en": "a new user object with that data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 25.17,
          "end": 27.76,
          "en": "and we add that to an array of users object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 27.76,
          "end": 30.74,
          "en": "which we then output in the users list.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 30.74,
          "end": 32.47,
          "en": "And how do we do that?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 32.47,
          "end": 33.303,
          "en": "Well for that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 33.303,
          "end": 37.37,
          "en": "we need this concept which was called lifting the state up.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 37.37,
          "end": 40.91,
          "en": "We need to manage our list of users in a place,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 40.91,
          "end": 44.59,
          "en": "where we can get both access to the AddUser component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 44.59,
          "end": 48.89,
          "en": "and well get notified when that AddUser button was clicked",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 48.89,
          "end": 50.85,
          "en": "as well as where we got access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 50.85,
          "end": 54.683,
          "en": "to the users list component to feed our users array into it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 55.78,
          "end": 58.18,
          "en": "And we don't have access to UsersList",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 58.18,
          "end": 60,
          "en": "inside of AddUser, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 60,
          "end": 62.12,
          "en": "So managing our Userslist,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 62.12,
          "end": 65.043,
          "en": "state here would be wrong our users array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 65.951,
          "end": 68.63,
          "en": "UsersList component sounds like the right place",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 68.63,
          "end": 71.12,
          "en": "because there we need that list,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 71.12,
          "end": 75.6,
          "en": "but there we don't get access to the added user data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 75.6,
          "end": 79.197,
          "en": "that AddUser form is out of reach here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 79.197,
          "end": 82.37,
          "en": "But actually we already configured this UsersList component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 82.37,
          "end": 84.99,
          "en": "to work differently and to get the users data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 84.99,
          "end": 87.44,
          "en": "from outside wire props.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 87.44,
          "end": 91.2,
          "en": "Because that's the place where we wanna manage our state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 91.2,
          "end": 93.85,
          "en": "We wanna manage it in the App.js component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 93.85,
          "end": 95.57,
          "en": "because that's the one component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 95.57,
          "end": 97.84700000000001,
          "en": "above both AddUser and UsersList,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 98.81,
          "end": 102.61,
          "en": "it's the nearest component above those two components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 102.61,
          "end": 104.91,
          "en": "which has access to both components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 104.91,
          "end": 107.36699999999999,
          "en": "And therefore we lift the state management",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 107.36699999999999,
          "end": 109.463,
          "en": "up to this App component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 110.72999999999999,
          "end": 114.03999999999999,
          "en": "So we wanna manage our users array here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 114.03999999999999,
          "end": 116.47,
          "en": "and we do this with the useState Hook of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 116.47,
          "end": 118.55,
          "en": "because it's state of this App,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 118.55,
          "end": 122.41,
          "en": "and when that state data changes, the App should rerender,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 122.41,
          "end": 124.58,
          "en": "and that's exactly what useState",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 124.58,
          "end": 127.43,
          "en": "and the state managed by it does.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 127.43,
          "end": 130.95,
          "en": "And therefore here, we call useState instead of App,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 130.95,
          "end": 133.433,
          "en": "and we initialize this with an empty array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 134.78,
          "end": 137.9,
          "en": "Now, as you learned, useState always returns two elements,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 137.9,
          "end": 140.34,
          "en": "so we can use a radius structuring,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 140.34,
          "end": 144.04,
          "en": "and we got our, let's say UsersList",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 144.04,
          "end": 147.373,
          "en": "and a set UsersList function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 148.55,
          "end": 152.24,
          "en": "And it's now the UsersList, which I wanna forward",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 152.24,
          "end": 154.253,
          "en": "to the UsersList component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 155.2,
          "end": 157.52,
          "en": "With that, it's still an empty array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 157.52,
          "end": 160.13,
          "en": "but we have a function that allows us to change",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 160.13,
          "end": 163.22,
          "en": "to the array and then that change would trigger",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 163.22,
          "end": 165.42000000000002,
          "en": "that App component to be rendered,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 165.42000000000002,
          "end": 169.07,
          "en": "and hence the UsersList component would be updated as well",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 169.07,
          "end": 170.94,
          "en": "because it would all also be rendered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 170.94,
          "end": 172.833,
          "en": "since it's part of the App component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 174.03,
          "end": 176.24,
          "en": "So now the missing piece is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 176.24,
          "end": 178.84,
          "en": "that when we click the AddUser button",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 178.84,
          "end": 182.87,
          "en": "and hence the AddUserHandler in the AddUser component runs,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 182.87,
          "end": 186.436,
          "en": "we foreward the enteredUsername",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 186.436,
          "end": 189.45,
          "en": "and the enteredAge to the App component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 189.45,
          "end": 191.39,
          "en": "And we do this with props as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 191.39,
          "end": 193.43,
          "en": "You'll learn this as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 193.43,
          "end": 195.69,
          "en": "We can add a prop here on AddUser",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 195.69,
          "end": 199.45,
          "en": "and we can name it however you want, for example, onAddUser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 199.45,
          "end": 202.84,
          "en": "And I just use this on something convention,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 202.84,
          "end": 205.85,
          "en": "because in the end it will kind of work like an event.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 205.85,
          "end": 208.96,
          "en": "Now we'll handle it fully ourselves,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 208.96,
          "end": 210.76,
          "en": "but at the end it is like an event.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 210.76,
          "end": 213.07999999999998,
          "en": "When that AddUser button is clicked,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 213.07999999999998,
          "end": 215.88,
          "en": "which ultimately happens when I click on the button,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 215.88,
          "end": 220.14,
          "en": "surprise, surprise, then a function which we pass to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 220.14,
          "end": 223.07,
          "en": "onAddUser should be triggered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 223.07,
          "end": 225.21,
          "en": "It's a function we have yet to define",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 225.21,
          "end": 226.6,
          "en": "and we can define it here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 226.6,
          "end": 230.55,
          "en": "The AddUserHandler here in the App component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 230.55,
          "end": 234.35,
          "en": "And that's a function where I actually expect two arguments,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 234.35,
          "end": 237.44,
          "en": "the userName and the userAge.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 237.44,
          "end": 238.91,
          "en": "And you can name these parameters",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 238.91,
          "end": 240.26,
          "en": "however you want of course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 241.58,
          "end": 243.28,
          "en": "I expect to get that data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 243.28,
          "end": 246.42,
          "en": "and with that data, we can create a new user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 246.42,
          "end": 248.91,
          "en": "and add it to our list here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 248.91,
          "end": 253.59,
          "en": "by calling setUsersList and then updating the state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 253.59,
          "end": 255.39,
          "en": "Now here, I wanna update the state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 255.39,
          "end": 259.28,
          "en": "by taking the old list and appending a new element to it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 259.28,
          "end": 261.52,
          "en": "And as you all learned earlier,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 261.52,
          "end": 265.41,
          "en": "when your state update relies on the previous state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 265.41,
          "end": 269.56,
          "en": "you wanna use an alternative form of set UsersList.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 269.56,
          "end": 271.55,
          "en": "You wanna use that function form,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 271.55,
          "end": 275.31,
          "en": "where you pass a function to setUsersList.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 275.31,
          "end": 278.29,
          "en": "And that function will automatically get the previous",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 278.29,
          "end": 283.29,
          "en": "latest state snapshot, when React perform state update here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 283.86,
          "end": 286.073,
          "en": "And therefore all named at prevUsersList,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 287.65999999999997,
          "end": 289.23,
          "en": "the name is up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 289.23,
          "end": 292.19,
          "en": "And you then should return your new state snapshot",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 292.19,
          "end": 296.83,
          "en": "in the body of this function you pass to setUsersList.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 296.83,
          "end": 300.3,
          "en": "So here I'll return an array, a new array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 300.3,
          "end": 301.44,
          "en": "where I first of all,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 301.44,
          "end": 304.343,
          "en": "copy all elements from prevUsersList,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 305.91,
          "end": 308.06,
          "en": "and that's the spread operator which simply",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 308.06,
          "end": 310.54,
          "en": "pulls all elements out of that array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 310.54,
          "end": 313.98,
          "en": "and adds them as new elements to this new array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 313.98,
          "end": 316.74,
          "en": "And then I add one new element at the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 316.74,
          "end": 319.06,
          "en": "I add a new JavaScript object here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 319.06,
          "end": 320.48,
          "en": "which should have a name field,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 320.48,
          "end": 323.94,
          "en": "uName is the value we stored there and the age field",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 323.94,
          "end": 326.61,
          "en": "which stores uAge as a value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 326.61,
          "end": 329.87,
          "en": "So the two values we get as parameters here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 329.87,
          "end": 330.76,
          "en": "And with that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 330.76,
          "end": 333.85,
          "en": "we treat a new JavaScript object for every user,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 333.85,
          "end": 337.173,
          "en": "and we add that to our UsersList array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 338.22,
          "end": 341.89,
          "en": "And now we just need to wire this up, addUserHandler",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 341.89,
          "end": 346.07,
          "en": "is what I pass to the onAddUser prop here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 346.07,
          "end": 348.62,
          "en": "on my AddUser component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 348.62,
          "end": 350.73,
          "en": "And now inside of the AddUser component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 350.73,
          "end": 354,
          "en": "we need to utilize this onAddUser prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 354,
          "end": 357.8,
          "en": "So here in AddUser, in the AddUserHandler there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 357.8,
          "end": 360.26,
          "en": "so inside of the AddUser component now,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 360.26,
          "end": 362.06,
          "en": "instead of console logging,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 362.06,
          "end": 364.703,
          "en": "I will call props dot onAddUser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 365.741,
          "end": 368.1,
          "en": "And I'll execute it as a function here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 368.1,
          "end": 371.64,
          "en": "because I know that what I get as a value on that prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 371.64,
          "end": 373.56,
          "en": "will be a function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 373.56,
          "end": 376.76,
          "en": "Because we're passing a pointer at AddUserHandler",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 376.76,
          "end": 381.42,
          "en": "to onAddUser and AddUserHandler is a function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 381.42,
          "end": 383.64,
          "en": "So we can execute it as a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 383.64,
          "end": 385.823,
          "en": "inside of the AddUser component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 386.93,
          "end": 390.57,
          "en": "And now we just have to forward our two pieces of data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 390.57,
          "end": 392.71,
          "en": "the enteredUsername and the enteredAge",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 394.461,
          "end": 397.235,
